-- chem/chargeclass.hypercubical — the electric energy on the graph depends only on the multiset of vertex charges,
-- not on where the charges sit or how far apart they are. Each vertex's lowest energy in its sector is a function of
-- its charge alone (chem/sectorcharge.hypercubical), so the total is the sum over vertices of that function, a sum
-- that is unchanged by reordering the vertices or by inserting neutral vertices between them. The edge holonomies
-- move charge from vertex to vertex (chem/edgehol, chem/pathtransport) without changing this multiset, so they leave
-- the electric energy fixed: it is a class function of the charge distribution, constant along every path the
-- holonomies can take. The force between charges is therefore absent from the electric term for every configuration,
-- not only a single pair (chem/pairenergy.hypercubical) — it lives entirely in the kinetic hop cost.
import "pairenergy.hypercubical"

